  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 20.8%, indicating RNA is the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether the PCA representation is already near-optimal for RNA or whether a learned encoder (scVI) can extract more discriminative signal. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates the RNA encoder choice as the single variable changed from config_001, directly testing if a learned, biologically-informed representation outperforms linear PCA. If scVI improves accuracy, it justifies investing further experiments in learned encoders and potentially multimodal fusion with a stronger RNA backbone. If it does not, PCA is sufficient and we can pivot to exploring multiprofile aggregation or multimodal fusion. With 7 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA representation early is critical because it underpins all multimodal configurations."
}

